[Example]
You order food → wait → food arrives.

[In programming]
Start request
     ↓
   Waiting...
     ↓
Data arrives

Promise means: I don't have the value right now, but I promise I'll give you the value later.

setTimeout(() => {}): don't immediately get the result.

resolve() means: The operation finished successfully. Here is the result.
reject() means: Something went wrong.

.then() means: When the Promise finishes, run this code.
